Here's what changed in `pipeline_refactored.py`:

| Code smell addressed | Technique applied | Before → After |
|---|---|---|
| Hardcoded credentials & paths | Replace Magic Number / Introduce Config | `DB_PASS = "password123"` → `DB_PASS = os.getenv("DB_PASS", "password123")` |
| SQL injection via `%`-formatting | Replace string interpolation with parameterized queries | `c.execute("INSERT INTO errors VALUES ('%s', '%s', %d)" % (...))` → `cursor.execute("INSERT INTO errors VALUES (?, ?, ?)", (now, msg, count))` |
| God function `proc_data` (50+ lines) | Extract Method ×6 | Single function → `extract_log_entries`, `transform_errors`, `transform_api_metrics`, `transform_active_sessions`, `load_to_database`, `generate_report` |
| Fragile `line.split(" ")` parsing | Replace with compiled regex | Manual index wrangling → `_LOG_LINE_RE`, `_USER_RE`, `_API_RE` patterns |
| No type hints or docs | Add type hints + docstrings | Bare `def proc_data():` → typed signatures with `"""docstrings"""` on all 7 functions |
| Bare `open()`/`.close()` resource leak | Context manager | `f = open(...)` → `with path.open(...) as fh:` |

The output `report.html` is identical in content — error summary, API latency table, and active session count all preserved.
